WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, we don´t
always have enough time

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.171
to cover all of the recent news,

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:08.475
so here with a recap is one
of our writers, Amber Ruffin,

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.011 size:75% position:38%
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
♫♫

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys,
things have been crazy!

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all, Hurricane Harvey
caused so much devastation

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.222
that I was like, "What?!"

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:25.225
Then Americans banded together

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
and raised millions
to help the victims,

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.896
and I was like, "What! What!"

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:33.433
Then they were like, "Oops.
Here come 18 more storms."

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:36.036 size:84% position:42%
And I was like, "What?"

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:40.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
And after Harvey, Trump didn´t
visit Houston right away,

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everyone was like,
"Wh-a-a-at?"

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then he did, and his wife
wore five-inch heels,

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:52.085
and I was like, "What...
kind of flood are <i>you </i>going to?"

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:57.023
Then she wore a FLOTUS hat,
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:57.023 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I found out
that hat is for sale.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:04.964 size:88% position:44%
And I was like, "Who...
else needs a FLOTUS hat?

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:08.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are literally
the only FLOTUS on Earth!"

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:12.105
That would be like if the
NBC store sold a hat that said,

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.373
"The black lady who works

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
for ´Late Night
with Seth Meyers.´"

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.977 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:22.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would you buy it?
Oh, you would? Okay.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:25.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then Nintendo announced
that Super Mario

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:29.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
is officially no longer
a plumber, and I was like...

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:32.258
[ To tune of "Overworld Theme" ]
♫ What, what, what,
what-what-what-what? ♫

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:36.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, no, then I got worried
for him and was like...

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.431
[ Tune of "Underworld Theme" ]
♫ What-what-what-what-what? ♫

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:42.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, but, seriously,
R.I.P., Plumber Mario.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:46.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ To the tune of "Game Over" ]
♫ What, what, what,
what-what, wh-a-a-at ♫

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then, uh...

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.676 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah!

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.979
[ Tune of "Underworld Theme" ]
♫ What-what-what-what-what? ♫

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.782 size:88% position:44%
Then I saw that in Utah,

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:59.586
that cop dragged that nurse out
of that hospital for no reason!

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:03.623
And I was like, "What...do you
think she is -- a black person?"

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.125 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:09.095
That´s not what we meant when
we were talking about equality.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:12.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, you know there are
no black people in your state

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.300
when even the nurses are white.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:19.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don´t want to buy
the hat anymore?

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:22.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s fine.
It wasn´t for sale anyway.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I read
astronaut Peggy Whitson

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.380 size:81% position:41%
just got back to Earth

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
after 665 days
of being off the planet.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.254
She must have gotten to Earth,
looked around, and been like,

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:38.725 size:81% position:41%
"What...the [bleep]?!"

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.760
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
♫♫

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.131
-Amber Ruffin, everybody.

